Once you’ve downloaded Spark AR Studio, you need to go through the tutorials of the interface of the program in the Learning Center and then make a decision about whether you want to choose from among eight templates or make a filter from scratch.
A placeholder object will appear in the central panel (viewport) if you choose a template. The Simulator where you can preview your work is the iPhone 8 that’s in the corner, but this can be changed to another device.
Upload a 3D asset You will then have to select a 3D asset for your AR filter, which you can either import on your own or select from the AR Library which has animations, free audio files, and a lot more.
With more experimentation, you’ll learn how to use this platform like a pro to create AR filters that are sure to capture the attention of your Instagram followers. Best practices
