While the essence of Instagram Live is quite similar to that of Facebook Live and YouTube Live, it consists of several features that make it unique and very promising for businesses. Let’s take a detailed look at them.
When you go live using the Instagram Live feature, it automatically becomes the first story to appear across your followers’ feeds. The success that the Instagram Stories feature has seen guarantees that a significant percentage of your Instagram followers will watch your live videos.
You’d think that they’ll miss out on your videos in such a situation, right?
By default, Instagram will notify your followers when you go live through push notifications. While followers have the option of disabling push notifications for live videos, the fact that it’s enabled by default means that more followers are likely to watch your videos.
This allows followers who missed out on your live video to catch up with your content later. While real-time engagement isn’t possible if people watch the video after the live broadcast ends, it still allows your live content to be viewed, enhancing brand awareness.
For businesses and brands that want to do Q&A sessions, there couldn’t be anything better. Using this basic collaboration feature, full-blown interviews and discussions can be conducted.
