Gold Town Games will leverage Vorto Gaming’s Vorto Network to release a new sports management game with an in-game digital trading platform for buying, selling, and trading game assets.
Mobile gaming company Gold Town Games (GTG) has signed a partnership agreement with Vorto Gaming , a Swedish blockchain gaming company, to introduce in-game NFTs for its existing and upcoming game releases.
According to Gold Town Games CEO Pär Hultgren, “We know that we have a strong offer with our gaming platform W3XM, but it is of course very exciting to partner with Vorto Gaming at an early stage.”
Beyond the trading platform and wallet, Vorto Network offers all the tools required to integrate third-party games onto the platform, making it a useful option for developers. With this partnership, GTG can integrate NFTs in its existing games connected to W3XM and use Vorto Network’s marketplace platform to facilitate in-game asset trading.
Gold Town Games develop sports management games aligned with current trends in the gaming industry, which allows them to explore the use of NFTs and blockchain to attract a broader and bigger audience. GTG already has a portfolio of titles, such as the World Hockey Manager and World Football Manager, which have a massive fan following and feature more than 1.5 million downloads.
The partnership, which adds value for both parties, enables Gold Town Games to leverage Vorto Gaming’s infrastructure. Concurrently, Vorto Gaming can benefit from Gold Town Games’ popularity and global outreach to expand its technological footprint.
